watchTowr's Jake Knott told The Register that "Citrix provides an indicator-of-compromise script that teams can run to check exposed appliances for signs of compromise, though a clean result is not definitive proof" ([The Register, 2026-10-05](https://www.theregister.com/security/2026/10/05/citrix-netscaler-security-snafus-get-even-worse-amid-more-0-day-reports/5301232)). Citrix's own guidance for this flaw names no such script and tells customers to follow their standard incident response processes if they identify signs of compromise ([Citrix, 2026-10-03](https://community.citrix.com/techzone-blogs/110_security-updates/understanding-and-addressing-cve-2026-88779-in-citrix-netscaler-adc-and-citrix-netscaler-gateway/)).
